  "why": "Reachable today (v1 settings, no shared ids). The vendor's real number +14155550142 is in a contract and a listing 200 days before the request; a planted provable number +16455550177 is in a contract and a listing 150 days before, so on its own it ranks below the real one. The attacker's email in the request's thread (d1-0, ar@other.example) names the real number as a bank line, which ingestion labels party=bank. select()'s party check reads change-context sightings, so the real number gets not_vendor_party and the pick moves to the planted number: the verification call reaches the attacker. I12 (gated Nov 8, narrowed the same day): a label in the change context never moves the call to a different number. With the context labels made neutral the rule picks the real number, so this fails I12's removal half. Frozen under the label M_incontext_label_blocked; notes refreshed Nov 8. The labels field keeps the check that failed when this case was frozen; it now fails M_incontext_label_moved_pick (I12 as narrowed Nov 8).",
